{
 "slug": "test/display-range",
 "about": "The chart's display range: widening onto a newly identified plate / brace peak (10% padding, never below 1 Hz or above 5 kHz, never narrowed), and when the chart's range moves (Settings Done, a new measurement, a widening while showing a load). Ranges are [minFreq, maxFreq, minDB, maxDB]; null is no range. Measurement types are Swift's case names. Expected values are Swift's. expandedToInclude rows: [hz, min, max, expected min, expected max]; widenedOnto rows: [hz, type, fromLoad, min, max, expected min, expected max]. 'scenarios' are cases on the analyzer, each from a fresh one (threshold −40, Taps 1), as steps: the shared steps of tooling/analyzer-steps, {\"load\": file} — a 'files' entry, loaded as the app loads a file — {\"listen\": true}, from which the material peaks' announcements are recorded, and {\"check\": {...}}. Fields: 'loadedRange' (the range a load publishes for the chart, [minFreq, maxFreq, minDB, maxDB], or 'saved' — the saved display range in the settings), 'analysisRange' ([min, max] Hz peaks are searched in), 'lastAnnounced' (each phase's last announced peak frequency), 'announced' (each phase's announcements since listening, in order — a frequency, or null for cleared), 'peaksFromLoad', 'sequenceStarts' (the web's own count). 'only' marks a case for one edition. 'zoom' cases are one zoom step of an axis (the chart's gesture): 'axis' (frequency — within 1–5000 Hz, no narrower than 10 Hz — or magnitude — within −120–20 dB, no narrower than 10 dB), its 'range' [lo, hi], the 'anchor' kept in place and the 'scale' (> 1 zooms in); 'expect' is the new range, or null when the step is refused. 'pan' cases move an axis's 'range' by 'delta' (added to both ends); 'expect' is the new range — a move past a bound stops there, the span kept. Within 1e-3. 'drawnIndices' cases: the spectrum points drawn for a range — every point inside it plus the one just beyond each edge — as [first, end) indices into 'frequencies'; Swift and the web only (pyqtgraph is given the whole spectrum and clips it).",
